==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-like shooting fish in a barrel.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Prepositional phrase===
{{en-PP}}

# {{lb|en|simile}} [[extremely|Extremely]] [[easy]].
#: {{syn|en|easy as pie|like taking candy from a baby|Thesaurus:easy}}
#* '''1982''' April 2, [[w:Associated Press|Associated Press]], "[http://news.google.com/newspapers?id=d-YbAAAAIBAJ&sjid=llIEAAAAIBAJ&pg=6967,218982&dq=like-shooting-fish-in-a-barrel&hl=en Entrants Gamble For Chance To Stalk Big Game]," ''The Dispatch'' (USA), p. 20 <small>(retrieved 18 July 2012)</small>:
#*: Opponents contend that the lumbering creatures are so easy to shoot that a moose hunt is a slaughter, not a sport. "It's '''like shooting fish in a barrel'''," they say.
#* '''2003''' Oct. 24, [[w:Ken Johnson (art critic)|Ken Johnson]], "[http://www.nytimes.com/2003/10/24/arts/art-in-review-mary-ellen-mark-twins.html Art in Review: Mary Ellen Mark—‘Twins’]," ''New York Times'' <small>(retrieved 18 July 2012)</small>:
#*: For a photographer, shooting twins at the annual Twins Days Festival in Twinsburg, Ohio, must be '''like shooting fish in a barrel'''.
#* '''2005''' March 29, John S. Doyle, "[http://www.independent.ie/unsorted/features/were-all-sport-crazy-but-for-all-the-wrong-sports-271307.html We're all sport crazy... but for all the wrong sports]," ''Irish Independent'' (Ireland) <small>(retrieved 18 July 2012)</small>:
#*: Standing on those long straight roads with the speed detection gun was '''like shooting fish in a barrel''', somebody said.

